---
/**
 * Architecture overview section component.
 * Owner: Scenario 4 - Architecture Overview Diagram
 *
 * Displays:
 * - LSM-tree data flow diagram (WAL -> Memtable -> SSTable)
 * - Component descriptions
 * - Link to detailed documentation
 */
---

<section class="architecture section" id="architecture">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="section-title">Architecture</h2>
    <div class="architecture-content">
      <div class="architecture-diagram">
        <pre class="diagram">{`
Write Request
    │
    ▼
┌─────────┐
│   WAL   │──── Write-Ahead Log for durability
└────┬────┘
     │
     ▼
┌──────────┐
│ Memtable │──── Active in-memory skip list
└────┬─────┘
     │ (when full)
     ▼
┌────────────────┐
│ Imm Memtables  │──── Immutable memtables queue
└───────┬────────┘
        │ (minor compaction)
        ▼
┌───────────────┐
│ Level 0 SSTs  │──── Recently flushed, may overlap
└───────┬───────┘
        │ (major compaction)
        ▼
┌───────────────┐
│ Level 1+ SSTs │──── Sorted, non-overlapping within level
└───────────────┘
        `}</pre>
      </div>
      <p class="architecture-description">
        MirDB uses a Log-Structured Merge-Tree (LSM-tree) architecture optimized for write-heavy workloads.
        All writes are first logged to the WAL for durability, then stored in an in-memory skip list (memtable).
        When the memtable fills up, it's flushed to disk as a Sorted String Table (SSTable).
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .architecture-content {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .architecture-diagram {
    background: var(--color-code-bg);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: var(--space-lg);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  .diagram {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    background: transparent;
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    line-height: 1.4;
    white-space: pre;
  }

  .architecture-description {
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    line-height: var(--line-height-relaxed);
  }
</style>
